.agents/
.codex/
skills-lock.json
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/
.github/skills/

# The impeccable detector's own config + cache. Same reasoning as .agents/ above:
# the tool is mine, not the product. The DECISIONS it records (which findings are
# accepted and why) live in docs/roadmap.md GA-2, which is committed — so the
# reasoning survives even though the machine-readable file does not.
.impeccable/

# The 4K masters behind the three /learn illustrations (2026-08-16). ~47 MB of
# lossless PNG, too heavy for git, and the site ships the 1600x1000 crops in
# web/public/learn/ instead.
#
# ⚠️ IRREPLACEABLE, and that is the whole reason they are kept at all. These are
# generated images and generation is NOT reproducible: the prompts are stored
# beside them and re-running one returns a DIFFERENT picture, not this one. So
# if this folder is lost, the only remaining copies of these exact images are
# the cropped, colour-corrected 1600x1000 versions that are committed — fine for
# the Learn bands, useless for a hero, a share card, a reframe or print.
#
# Ignored, not deleted. Back it up with the owner's own files, not with git.
reference/learn-masters/

# Excel writes a lock file beside any workbook it has open. The article working
# file is reviewed while it is being rebuilt, so this appears and disappears.
~$*
